            new("OnCellSave", "After a cell's value is written: when the batch editor commits on Enter, Tab, blur or a click elsewhere, when a checkbox toggles, and when a context-menu paste or delete, a type-ahead commit or a fill writes a value. Also raised when a touched editor commits the text it started with, so a row can be marked dirty without a change; an untouched editor that commits because focus moved, and an edit abandoned with Escape, raise nothing. There is no cancel: the value is already in the row.", "CellSaveArgs&lt;TValue&gt;"),
